// v0.13.0 D5: bare const-prefixed functions are rejected by name —
// const has no meaning on a function (functions are not rebindable;
// const-aggregate immutability is a type-level concept). The shape
// used to die at the body/param tokens with a generic syntax error.
const int f(int x) {
    return x;
}
int main() { return 0; }
